      initial: 'off',
      description: 'Engine throttle with detents at OFF, IDLE, MIL and MAX AB. OFF stops engine ignition and fuel flow; between OFF and IDLE the throttle is rolled outboard to pass the cutoff. IDLE commands minimum thrust and is used for all ground and air starts. From IDLE to MIL the throttle sets engine output; forward of MIL it controls the afterburner.',
